From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: A window on another screen keeps the phone's overview

Plinius: the first window folded the overview on every screen count. With a second screen (the
desktop over VNC) a window started there left the phone with only its wallpaper: no app, no app
grid. A start from the app grid still folds it, that goes through activity-launched.
---
 src/shell.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/shell.c b/src/shell.c
index 4cae9ff2..35d252ff 100644
--- a/src/shell.c
+++ b/src/shell.c
@@ -853,7 +853,9 @@ on_toplevel_added (PhoshShell *self, PhoshToplevel *unused, PhoshToplevelManager
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_TOPLEVEL_MANAGER (toplevel_manager));
 
   priv = phosh_shell_get_instance_private (self);
-  if (phosh_toplevel_manager_get_num_toplevels (toplevel_manager) == 1)
+  /* With a second screen the window may be on the other one: the phone keeps its overview */
+  if (phosh_toplevel_manager_get_num_toplevels (toplevel_manager) == 1 &&
+      phosh_monitor_manager_get_num_monitors (priv->monitor_manager) <= 1)
     phosh_home_set_state (PHOSH_HOME (priv->home), PHOSH_HOME_STATE_FOLDED);
 }
 
